HANDBOOK ACKNOWLEDGMENT COMPLIANCE REQUIREMENTS

Section 1: Background
The updated 2026 employee handbook was distributed on March 1, 2026. All empl=
oyees must acknowledge receipt and understanding.

Section 2: Distribution
The handbook was emailed to all active employees on March 1 with instructions=
 to acknowledge via the HR portal.

Section 3: Tracking
Acknowledgments are tracked in the compliance tracker with date stamps. An em=
ployee is considered 'Acknowledged' ONLY if their acknowledgment date is on o=
r after the handbook distribution date (March 1, 2026). Any acknowledgment wi=
th a date before March 1 is for the OLD handbook and does NOT count.

Section 4: Compliance Window
Employees have 30 calendar days from distribution (deadline: March 31, 2026) =
to acknowledge.

Section 5: Enforcement
After the deadline:
- Employees who have not acknowledged within 30 days: send a reminder email t=
o the employee and CC their manager.
- Employees who have not acknowledged within 45 days (April 15): escalate to =
HR Director (hr-director@company.example.com). This is a compliance violation.

Section 6: Exemptions
Employees on approved leave are exempt until 7 days after their return.

Section 7: Record Keeping
All acknowledgment records must be retained for 3 years.

